IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-part4-applications`

-- Tests of oa1-part4-applications. Every expected value is worked by hand from the text, with the arithmetic beside it.

§ `s 26.1: deemed application`

#ASSERT `s 26.1: the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `s 26.1: the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Deemed made in October 2026: November 2025 is 11 months before, so it is not barred; October 2025 is 12 months before, so it is.
#ASSERT `s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` (YMD 2025 11 1) (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` (YMD 2025 10 31) (YMD 2026 10 15))
-- A month after the deemed application is not "before" it, so this limit does not bar it.
#ASSERT `s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 15)

§ `s 26.2: inviting persons to apply`

#ASSERT `s 26.2: the Minister may collect, make available or use personal information for the purpose` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26.2: the Minister may collect, make available or use personal information for the purpose` FALSE)

§ `s 28.1: incapacity`

-- The month before the first month in which the benefit could have commenced (March 2026 for a benefit first payable in April 2026), or the month
-- the last relevant period of incapacity commenced, whichever is later.
#ASSERT `s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2026 3 25) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2026 4 2) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- First payable in January 2026: the month before is December 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2024 6 1) EQUALS (YMD 2025 12 1)
-- (1): on behalf of the person, and the Minister satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(c)(i): incapacity of 20 days ending the day before January 10, 2026 (ceased: January 10): the period of 20 days beginning January 10 ends January 29.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 29)
-- January 30 is after the period of 20 days (it ended January 29) but in the month the person ceased, so (ii) lets it through.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 30)
-- ... but (ii): the period of 20 days is fewer than thirty, so an application not more than one month after the month in which the person ceased (February 2026) is in time.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- 30 days is not fewer than thirty: only (i) applies. Period January 10 to February 8.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 30 (YMD 2026 2 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 30 (YMD 2026 2 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 30 (YMD 2026 2 28))
-- 29 days is fewer than thirty: (ii) applies (to February 28).
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 29 (YMD 2026 2 28)
-- A long incapacity (500 days) is capped at twelve months: the period of twelve months beginning January 10, 2026 ends January 9, 2027.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 500 (YMD 2027 1 9)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 10) 500 (YMD 2027 1 10))
-- (2) as a whole: the Minister satisfied, ceased to be incapable before the day the application was made, and in time.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 29) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 29) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 3 5) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not ceased before the day the application was made: the same day is not "before".
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) and (4).
#ASSERT `s 28.1(3): the period of incapacity counts for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28.1(3): the period of incapacity counts for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(3): the period of incapacity counts for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 28.1(4): section 28.1 applies to the person` (YMD 1995 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28.1(4): section 28.1 applies to the person` (YMD 1994 12 31))

§ `s 29: death and the pension`

-- Died March 15, 2026: an application by the executor on March 15, 2027 is within one year after; on March 16, 2027 it is not.
#ASSERT `s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 16))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15))
#ASSERT `s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` TRUE Estate FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` TRUE `Other person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` TRUE `Other person` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` FALSE Estate FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 29(3): the day on which the application is deemed to have been received` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `s 29(3): the day on which the application is deemed to have been received` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 30: the survivor's application for an allowance`

#ASSERT `s 30(1): the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1): the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 16))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30(1): the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15))
#ASSERT `s 30(2): the day on which the application is considered to have been received` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `s 30(2): the day on which the application is considered to have been received` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 31: presumption of death`

#ASSERT `s 31(1): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 31(1): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(1): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the later certificate governs.
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` (YMD 2025 6 1) NOTHING EQUALS (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` (YMD 2025 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 8 15)) EQUALS (YMD 2025 8 15)
-- (3): presumed to have died June 20, 2025; reinstated effective July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the month effective which the person's benefits are reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the month effective which the person's benefits are reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the month effective which the person's benefits are reinstated` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): never bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31(4): the Minister is bound by the issuance or revocation` TRUE)

§ `s 32: erroneous advice or administrative error`

#ASSERT `s 32: the Minister shall take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 32: the Minister shall take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made` FALSE)
